    "programmeDescription": "Econometrics and Operations Research at Erasmus University Rotterdam combines a substantial mathematical and statistical core with programming, econometrics, economics and operations research. The reviewed 2026–2027 route adds the Econometrics major, open profiling space, ethics, career preparation and a major-linked bachelor thesis.",
    "comparisonExplanation": "Three UCR programmes offer related study through quantitative economics and optimisation, econometrics with data science, or quantitative economics and finance. Each provides sustained mathematics, statistics, programming and economic analysis. Software construction, probabilistic decision models and numerical methods contribute defined additional skills. UCR has one dedicated econometrics course and does not reproduce the full advanced econometrics, time-series, simulation, major seminar or thesis sequence.",
