      "routeLabel": "Dutch-language, full-time; Econometrics major",
      "limitation": "The selected 2026–2027 Econometrics path includes Advanced Econometrics, Quantitative Methods for Data Science and Seminar in Forecasting. It retains 12 EC of minor space and 12 EC of electives, plus two one-credit Career Skills components. The individual thesis follows the major seminar; Ethics in Econometrics is required beforehand."
    },
    "cellNotes": [
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-1",
        "reference": "BENECON312",
        "text": "Econometrics covers regression-based estimation, testing, causal analysis and prediction in Stata. It is one dedicated course, not the comparator's multi-course econometrics and time-series sequence."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-2",
        "reference": "BENECON312",
        "text": "Econometrics provides the dedicated econometric core; machine learning, statistics and neural networks broaden predictive modelling but do not replace advanced econometrics or time-series analysis."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-3",
        "reference": "BENECON312",
        "text": "Econometrics supplies regression and inference. The finance route adds accounting, banking and investment context but does not offer the comparator's specialist Quantitative Finance major."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-1",
        "reference": "DISARIN311",
        "text": "Optimization Methods in AI studies local/global and first- and second-order optimisation, search, constraints and discrete methods. It supplies substantive optimisation study in an AI setting, without reproducing the complete operations-research sequence."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-2",
        "reference": "BENBUSI211",
        "text": "The course analyses the business, economic, governance and ethical implications of AI. It supplies application context, not technical data-science or econometric methods."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-3",
        "reference": "BENBUSI112",
        "text": "Accounting & Corporate Finance includes financial and management accounting, financial-statement analysis and investment appraisal using discounted cash flow. It supports financial decisions but does not provide specialist financial econometrics."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-3",
        "reference": "BENGATE101",
        "text": "Entrepreneurship & Business Foundations adds venture and business-planning context; it does not contribute quantitative-finance methods."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-1",
        "reference": "ACCPPDE101",
        "text": "PPD develops academic writing, research literacy and presenting through literature work and a community project. It is introductory and does not reproduce econometric academic communication or the Career Skills job-market programme."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-2",
        "reference": "ACCPPDE101",
        "text": "PPD develops academic writing, research literacy and presenting through literature work and a community project. It is introductory and does not reproduce econometric academic communication or the Career Skills job-market programme."
      },
      {
        "programmeId": "ucr-3",
        "reference": "ACCPPDE101",
        "text": "PPD develops academic writing, research literacy and presenting through literature work and a community project. It is introductory and does not reproduce econometric academic communication or the Career Skills job-market programme."
      }
